cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use laMEG in your research, please cite the software and the methodological publication(s) relevant to the analyses you use."
title: "laMEG: a toolbox for laminar inference with MEG"
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-07"

authors:
  - family-names: "Bonaiuto"
    given-names: "James J."

abstract: >-
  laMEG is an open-source Python toolbox for depth-resolved and laminar
  inference from magnetoencephalography (MEG) data. It provides tools for
  constructing multilayer cortical surface models, MEG and OPM-MEG forward
  modelling, laminar source reconstruction and model comparison, simulation,
  source-data export, and analysis of cortical-depth-resolved activity.

keywords:
  - magnetoencephalography
  - MEG
  - OPM-MEG
  - laminar neuroimaging
  - cortical depth
  - source reconstruction
  - neuroimaging
  - neuroscience

license: GPL-3.0-only
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21637876
repository-code: "https://github.com/danclab/laMEG"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/lameg/"
url: "https://danclab.github.io/laMEG/"